# an alias line points from the new name to the word it names, either way round (decision alias-arrows, card
# alias-arc-cosine): `alias twice => double` and `alias double <= twice` both make twice(…) call double
'double(x) := 2*x; alias twice => double; twice(4)'	8
'double(x) := 2*x; alias double <= twice; twice(4)'	8
'alias twice => double; double(x) := 2*x; twice(5)'	10
# a plain = says no direction: refused, its fix names the arrow
'double(x) := 2*x; alias twice = double; twice(4)'	error	no direction, refused
# the aliases of the library still name their words
'acos(1.0)'	0
'keys({a: 1, b: 2})'	['a', 'b']
'size([1, 2, 3])'	3
